# Commit identities permitted in this repository's history.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. On 2026-09-09 a test fixture wrote a throwaway
# identity into the real repository's .git/config — git honours an
# inherited GIT_DIR over its own `-C`, so a fixture running from inside a
# hook writes to the repo it was launched from. 151 commits were authored
# by it before anyone noticed, 96 of them pushed, where they surfaced as
# anonymous entries in the public contributor list.
#
# A pre-commit hook cannot prevent that recurring: hooks are client-side,
# opt-in here (`make hooks`), skippable with --no-verify, and never run on
# GitHub at all. This file is the server-side half — commit-identity.yml
# checks every pushed commit against it.
#
# One email per line. Comments and blank lines ignored. Matching is on the
# EMAIL only, because display names vary legitimately and carry no
# authority; the email is what GitHub attributes a contribution to.
